  <article class="article">
    <p class="eyebrow">Rust</p>
    <h1>What I'm learning in Rust right now</h1>
    <div class="article-copy">
      <p>I am working through Rust from the beginning instead of jumping straight into a large project. Right now that means ownership, borrowing, error handling, and tests.</p>
      <h2>Why I am keeping it small</h2>
      <p>It is easy to make a project look impressive before I understand it. Smaller programs force me to explain what each part does and make it obvious when I am guessing.</p>
      <h2>What comes next</h2>
      <p>I want to build a few command-line and file-parsing tools before moving into APIs, networking, and concurrency. The goal is to earn the harder projects instead of rushing into them.</p>
    </div>
